@startuml
!include ../shortfall/style.iuml
title generate-plan: combining typed and saved targets
autonumber

participant "MishMash" as App
participant "generate: GeneratePlanCommand" as Gen
participant "settings: TargetSettings" as Settings
participant "saved: NutritionTargets" as Saved
participant "planner: DietaryPlanner" as Planner
participant "activePlan: ActiveMealPlan" as Active

note over App, Gen : Parsing produced request = (days, typed targets); nutrients the user left out are null.
App -> Gen : execute(recipeBook)
activate Gen
Gen -> Settings : get()
Settings --> Gen : saved
alt nothing is saved
  note over Gen : effective = request, exactly as typed
else something is saved
  Gen -> Saved : overriddenBy(request.targets())
  Saved --> Gen : merged targets (a typed value wins; a gap keeps the saved value)
  note over Gen : effective = new GeneratePlanRequest(days, merged targets)
end
Gen -> Planner : generate(recipes, effective, dietary preferences)
activate Planner
alt no acceptable plan
  Planner --> Gen : throws IllegalArgumentException
  Gen --> App : throws MishMashException (the generator's message)
  note over Gen, Active : The previous active plan is left unchanged.
else plan found
  Planner --> Gen : plan
  deactivate Planner
  Gen -> Active : setGenerated(plan, effective, Optional.empty())
  Gen --> App : confirmation
end
deactivate Gen

note over Gen, Active
  The stored request holds the targets that were applied, so view-plan warnings and the repair done by
  set-diet use them instead of only the typed ones. TargetSettings is never modified here.
end note
@enduml
